Hearing this sorrowful melody, Vuli, a celestial fox woven of moonlight and biting winter wind, emerged. He was the silent sentinel of the earth’s greatest secret: deep beneath the frozen crust slept vast oceans of liquid light, the colorful, untamed dreams of all slumbering life. Moved by Aethel’s haunting music, Vuli began a fierce, rhythmic dance. His silver paws struck the frozen earth like hammers, cracking the world’s shell and releasing towering geysers of emerald, sapphire, and amethyst energy.

